Condition : 7 - No development (except demolition, archaeological investigations, ground condition investigations and intrusive site surveys and other enabling works: site clearance; soil storage; remedial works in respect of any contamination or any other adverse ground conditions; erection of any temporary means of enclosure and land raising) shall take place on the relevant phase (see plan 074_PL_004 Rev A) until details and samples of all facing materials to buildings relevant to that Phase are submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The samples and details shall include:
- brick/stonework (including brick/stone and mortar on-site sample panel min.
2m x 2m);
- cladding materials (including system specifications/details and on-site samples (where relevant);
- window treatment (including sections/reveals and on-site sample);
- all privacy measures, (including obscure glazing details, privacy screens, including measures to limit overlooking to 104 Pears Road on the eastern elevation of Block B etc.);
- balustrading treatment (including details/sections/materials for each balcony type);
- any other materials/details to be used including extract vents, boiler flues,
etc.; and
- the external treatment of flank walls of the maisonettes within podium of Block A.
Each phase of the development shall then be carried out in accordance with the approved details and maintained as such thereafter.

Condition : 24 - Prior to the commencement of any Phase (see plan 074_PL_004 A) of the development (except demolition, archaeological investigations, ground condition investigations and intrusive site surveys and other enabling works: site clearance; soil storage; remedial works in respect of any contamination or any other adverse ground conditions; erection of any temporary means of enclosure and land raising), details of both hard and soft landscape works for that Phase shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The works shall then be carried out as approved.
The detailed landscaping scheme shall include:
- soft planting: including any grass and turf areas, trees, planters, shrub and herbaceous areas including details of species, sizes, numbers/densities and sections of landscaped areas;
- a 'Tree Planting Statement' providing full details, locations, specifications and construction methods for all purpose-built tree pits and associated above ground features, including specifications for tree protection and a stated volume of suitable growing medium to facilitate and promote the healthy development of the proposed trees, ensuring each tree has a soil volume equivalent of 0.6 times its canopy area at maturity;
- hard landscaping: including ground surfaces, kerbs, edges, ridge and flexible paving, furniture, steps, refuse disposal points and if applicable synthetic surfaces for both ground level and roof terrace level (where relevant);
- delivery/loading areas associated with each residential block entrance to allow sufficient space for deliveries to be taken at the entrance;
- fences and walls and any other boundary treatments;
- any play spaces and play equipment (to the equivalent provision of 1,350sqm);
- any signage (Legible London) and information boards;
- brown (biodiversity) roofs/green walls (where relevant);
- any CCTV equipment;
- an external lighting strategy; and
